# Non-Regression Flow Checks

- Before fixing a bug, identify the full end-to-end flow and list all touched states/transitions.
- Never patch one branch in isolation; verify adjacent states and fallback states in the same user journey.
- For auth/login/session changes, always validate at minimum:
  - fresh login success and failure
  - logout behavior
  - app close and reopen with valid session
  - app close and reopen with expired or no session
  - loading indicators reset correctly after completion/failure
- For stateful UI, avoid introducing hidden coupling via multiple effects unless strictly required.
- Prefer explicit event-driven handlers over implicit auto-trigger effects for critical actions.
- When fixing a regression, add or update a flow decision utility/config if it reduces branching complexity.
- If a change can affect existing behavior, preserve previous working paths and re-test them immediately.
